      "content": "that makes sense. it feels like the only way to actually \"hear\" what my body is trying to do. \n\nbut i'm a little worried about the risks. if i'm going into total darkness and silence for long stretches, how do i differentiate between the biological \"calibration\" you're talking about and just... losing my grip? like, if i start seeing patterns or feeling intense rushes of energy while in the dark, how can i be sure that's actually my nervous system remapping itself rather than just my brain reacting to the lack of stimulus? are there any specific biological markers or ways to verify that this is a successful evolutionary step?",
      "source": "evaluator"
